$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B (in the absence of ligand,
Table 2) In a glovebox, aryl- or heteroarylboronic acid neopentylglycol
ester (1.0 mmol), aryl- or heteroaryl iodide (1.0 mmol), CsF (228 mg, 1.5
mmol) and CuI (3.8 mg, 0.020 mmol) were weighed in a 15-mL pressure
vessel and dissolved in DMF (5 mL). The pressure vessel was then tightly
capped, taken out of the glovebox and placed in an oil bath preheated to
120 °C with vigorous stirring. After 24 h, the reaction mixture was
cooled down to room temperature, diluted with ethyl acetate (15 mL) and
washed with H2O (5 mL × 3). The aqueous fraction was extracted back with
ethyl acetate (5 mL × 3) and combined with the first ethyl acetate
fraction. The combined ethyl acetate fraction was dried over Na2SO4 and
the solvent was removed in a rotary evaporator. The product was purified
by silica gel column chromatography using 10–20% ethylacetate/hexanes as
an eluting solvent. The title compound 39 was obtained as a white solid
(188 mg, 82% yield) after purification by silica gel column
chromatography. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.16 (m, 2H), 7.27 (t, J = 8.1
Hz, 1H), 7.48 (m, 3H), 7.62 (s, 1H), 8.31 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 106.2, 111.7, 117.6, 119.2, 121.9, 123.7, 126.3, 128.3,
140.4, 150.3, 151.7, 152.5, 155.5; HRMS (APPI) Calcd for C13H9ClNO (MH)+
230.0373, found 230.0376.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM copper-catalyzed Suzuki-Miyaura coupling, sealed pressure vial
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-Catalyzed Suzuki-Miyaura Coupling of Arylboronate Esters:
Transmetalation with (PN)CuF and Identification of Intermediates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gurung, Santosh K.; Thapa, Surendra; Kafle, Arjun; Dickie, Diane A.;
Giri, Ramesh
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(4), 1264-1267

