$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-(((3S,3aS)-1-oxo-7-(thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(35). A mixture of 33a (341 mg, 1 mmol), 2 N cesium carbonate (1 mL, 2
mmol), thiophene-2-boronic acid (192 mg, 1.5 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (120 mg, 0.1 mmol) in THF (30
mL) was degassed and flushed with argon. The mixture was hearted to
reflux for 24 h. Dichloromethane (100 mL) was added, and the mixture was
filtered through Celite, washed with water, saturated brine, dried over
sodium sulfate, and evaporated. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel with dichloromethane /methanol (100:1) to
give 35.
N-(((3S,3aS)-1-oxo-7-(pyridin-3-yl)-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(43). Compound 43 (278 mg, 82%) was prepared from 33a (341 mg, 1 mmol)
and pyridine-3-boronic acid (184 mg, 1.5 mmol) in the same manner as
described for 35. Mp: 193-194 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.79 (d, J =
2.06 Hz, 1 H), 8.57 (dd, J1 = 1.39 Hz, J2 = 4.77 Hz, 1 H), 8.08 (d, J =
8.36 Hz, 1H), 7.82 (m,1 H), 7.35 (dd, J1 = 4.77 Hz, J2 = 7.91 Hz, 1 H),
7.16-7.22 (m, 2 H), 6.36 (t, J = 6.23 Hz, 1 H), 4.59 (dd, J1 = 2.49 Hz,
J2 = 9.96 Hz, 1 H), 4.45 (m, 1 H), 3.90-4.05 (m, 2 H), 3.70-3.80 (m, 2
H), 2.06 (s, 3 H). Anal. Calcd for C18H17N3O4: C, 63.71; H, 5.05; N,
12.38. Found: C, 63.46; H, 4.93; N, 12.13. MS (EI) m/z: 339 (M+).
