$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
8-(2-methoxypyridin-3-yl)-3,6-dihydro-2H-furo[2,3-e]indole-7-carboxylate
(IIa). 2-Methoxypyridin-3-ylboronic acid (3.0 eq, 240 mg) was added to a
solution of 8-iodo-3,6-dihydro-2H-1-oxa-6-aza-as-indacene-7-carboxylic
acid methyl ester Ia (180 mg; 0.524 mmol) in 10 mL of
1,2-dimethoxyethane. The mixture was degassed (vaccum/argon flush) and
PdCl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2 (10 mol%, 42 mg) was added and the resulting orange
solution was stirred for 15 min at room temp. A solution of potassium
carbonate (6.0 eq, 3.1 mL of aq 1M soln) was added and the resulting
brown solution was stirred at 90 °C for 45 min at which time TLC (25%
ethyl acetate in hexanes) showed complete consumption of starting
material. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temp and diluted with
ethyl acetate (80 mL), washed with aq saturated sodium bicarbonate (10
mL) and brine (10 mL). The organic layer was dried over magnesium
sulfate, filtered and concentrated in rotavap. The product was purified
on silica gel (Biotage 25-S column; gradient: 10 to 50% ethyl acetate in
hexanes) to give the product. (3S)-Methyl
8-(2-methoxypyridin-3-yl)-3-methyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-furo[2,3-e]indole-7-carboxylate,
yield 130 mg, 82%. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, in DMSO-d6): δ 11.94 (1H, s), 8.12
(1H, dd, J = 2.19, 5.12 Hz), 7.64 (1H, dd, J = 2.19, 7.32 Hz), 7.13 (1H,
d, J = 8.05 Hz), 7.00 (1H, dd, J = 5.12, 7.32 Hz), 6.98 (1H, d, J = 8.05
Hz), 4.61 (1H, t, J = 8.78 Hz), 3.98 (1H, t, J = 8.05 Hz), 3.75 (3H, s),
3.68 (3H, s), 3.49 (1H, m), 1.22 (3H, d, J = 6.59 Hz). 13C-NMR (125 MHz,
in DMSO-d6): δ 161.4, 161.1, 152.6, 145.1, 140.3, 137.7, 123.2, 120.9,
120.8, 117.8, 116.0, 114.6, 113.3, 104.3, 78.8, 52.8, 51.3, 35.5, 19.9
ppm. LRMS (ESI): calcd. for C19H19N2O4 [M+H]+ 339.13, found 339.17.
