$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-(4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-
yl)-5-trimethylsilylthiophene (2). n-BuLi (2.34 M in hexane, 1.65 mL,
3.86 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was added to 2-bromo-5-trimethylsilylthiophene (1)
(0.8660 g, 3.68 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in THF (30 mL) at -78 °C. After 2 h at
-78 °C, the reaction mixture was treated with bis(pinacolato)diboron
(1.0280 g, 4.05 mmol, 1.1 equiv, dissolved in 15 mL of THF) and then
warmed slowly to ambient temperature overnight. The reaction mixture was
quenched with water, extracted with chloroform (3 × 40 mL), and finally
dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After the solvent was removed in vacuo, the
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel via gradient
elution using the solvent mixture (5:1 petroleum ether to chloroform) as
eluent. 2 (0.8517 g, 82%) as a white solid. Mp: 89-90 °C (lit.24 mp 61-62
°C). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.69 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (d, J =
3.2 Hz, 1H), 1.34 (s, 12H), 0.32 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
148.45, 137.86, 135.00, 84.02, 24.73, -0.11. IR (KBr): 3054, 2982, 2958,
2897 (C-H) cm-1. HRMS (EI+): m/z calcd for [C13H23O2SSi10B] 281.1317,
found 281.1314.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of Cyclooctatetrathiophenes with Different
Connection Sequences
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
