$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-annulated perylene monobromide 3 (735 mg, 1.08 mmol), boronic ester 4
(785 mg, 1.08 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (62 mg, 0.05 mmol) and Cs2CO3 (1.40 g,
4.30 mmol) were added into three-neck bottle under argon. Then degassed
toluene (50 mL) and DMF (2 mL) were added and purged with argon. The
mixture was stirred for 24 hours at 90 °C. After reaction finished and
cooled to room temperature, water was added. The product was extracted
with ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL). The organic layer was washed with
saturated brine and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed
under vacuum and the residue was purified by column chromatography
(silica gel, DCM: hexane = 1:5) to give a solid product (1.06 g, 82%),
yellow solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ 8.72 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 8.69
(d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 8.18 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 8.05 (s, 2H), 7.97 (d, J =
8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.88-7.81 (m, 6H), 7.64 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 4.59 (m, 4H),
2.32 (m, 2H), 1.39 (m, 12H), 1.18-1.09 (m, 68H), 0.88-0.83 (m, 12H). 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz): δ 136.49, 132.34, 132.22, 130.52, 129.40, 128.84,
124.96, 124.86, 124.57, 124.45, 123.61, 120.78, 120.73, 117.60, 117.04,
113.55, 50.21, 40.02, 31.90, 31.85, 31.82, 29.94, 29.90, 29.60, 29.56,
29.51, 29.31, 29.26, 26.51, 26.46, 22.66, 22.62, 14.08; HRMS (MALDI-TOF,
m/z): caldc for C88H116N2, 1200.9133; found, 1200.9167 (error = + 2.8
ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
