$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Suzuki-Miyaura
Cross-Couplings (A). In an oven-dried Schlenk tube backfilled with argon,
a mixture of nucleoside 2 (1.0 equiv), boronic acid or ester (1.5 equiv),
AcOK (1.5 equiv), Pd(dppf)Cl2 (0.05 equiv), was heated at 90˚C in dioxane
(0.08M) for 18h. The reaction was cooled to room temperature and diluted
with CH2Cl2. The solution was filtered through a pad of Celite and
extensively washed with CH2Cl2. The filtrate was concentrated under
reduced pressure and the residual oil was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel to provide biaryl nucleosides 6a-h.
1’-(3’-O-tertbutyldimethylsilyl-5’-O-triisopropylsilyl-2’-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranoside)-6-phenylquinazoline-2,4-(3H)-dione
(6a). According to the general procedure A, the biaryl nucleoside 6a was
obtained after column chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc, 90:10 →
85:15) using nucleoside 2 (0.400 g, 0.637 mmol), phenylboronic acid
(0.117 g, 0.956 mmol), AcOK (0.094 g, 0.956 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2 (0.026
g, 0.032 mmol).
1’-(3’-O-tertbutyldimethylsilyl-5’-O-triisopropylsilyl-2’-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranoside)-6-(N-methyl-2-pyrrole)-quinazoline-2,4-(3H)-dione
(6f). According to the general procedure A, the biaryl nucleoside 6f was
obtained after column chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc, 80:20 →
70:30) using nucleoside 2 (0.400 g, 0.637 mmol),
N-methyl-2-pyrroleboronic acid pinacol ester (0.330 g, 1.593 mmol), AcOK
(0.156 g, 1.593 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2 (0.026 g, 0.032 mmol). White foam,
0.327 g, 82%. Rf(hexane/EtOAc, 8:2): 0.24; [α]D26+38.9 (c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 9.54 (s, 1H), 8.24 (d, J1 = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 7.84 (d,
J1 = 8.8 Hz, 1H),7.65 (dd, J1 = 8.8 Hz, J2 = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 6.83 (t, J1 =
7.8 Hz, 1H, H1’), 6.75 (dd, J1 = 2.4 Hz, J2 = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 6.29 (dd, J1
=3.6 Hz, J2 = 1.8 Hz, 1H), 6.22 (dd, J1 = 3.6 Hz, J2 = 2.7 Hz, 1H),
4.80-4.76 (m, 1H, H3’), 4.08 (dd, J1 = 11.4 Hz, J2 = 2.8 Hz, 1H, H5’),
3.97 (dd, J1 = 11.4 Hz, J2 = 3.2 Hz, 1H, H5’), 3.88-3.87 (m, 1H, H4’),
3.71 (s, 3H), 2.86-2.78 (m, 1H, H2’),2.09 (ddd, J1 = 13.4 Hz, J2 = 7.4
Hz, J3 = 3.7 Hz, 1H, H2’), 1.23-1.11 (m, 21H), 0.92 (s, 9H), 0.11 (s,
3H), 0.10 (s, 3H);13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 162.0, 150.2, 138.3, 134.7,
132.5, 129.1, 127.5, 124.7, 117.4, 117.0, 109.5, 108.3, 86.6, 84.1, 70.2,
62.0, 37.1, 35.4, 25.9, 18.2, 12.1, -4.4, -4.7; IR (neat) ν: 3188, 3067,
2944, 2864, 1687, 1500,1459, 1318, 1109, 1057, 834, 777, 729, 509 cm-1;
HR-ESI MS (m/z): [M + Na]+ calcd for C33H53N3O5Si2Na 650.34160, found
650.34150.
