$DATUM 4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(5-(2-bromo-3-trifluoromethanesulfonate)pyridine-6-yl)-thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-
dioxaborolane (17)
4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(5-(trimethylstannyl)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(374 mg, 1.00 mmol), [Pd(PPh3)4] (23 mg, 2 mol%) and the
2-bromo-6-iodopyridin-3-yl trifluoromethane-sulfonate (432 mg, 1.00 mmol)
were dissolved in DMF (4 mL). The mixture was heated to 100 °C in a
microwave for 300 min and was then filtered over a short plug of celite.
The solvent was removed in vacuo and the crude product was purified by
column chromatography (n-hexanes/ethyl acetate (9:1). The product as a
colorless solid in a yield of 420 mg (82 %). Rf = 0.42; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 7.72 (d, 1H, 3 J = 3.7 Hz, Tph-H), 7.64 - 7.61 (m, 2H,
Pyr-H), 7.61 (d, 1H, 3 J = 3.7 Hz, Tph-H), 1.36 (s, 12H, pin-C(CH 3)4)
ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 155.5 (Pyr-C-h), 152.4 (Tph-C-d),
147.1 (Pyr-C-e), 142.9 (OTf-C), 137.9 (Tph-CH), 135.3 (Pyr-C-i), 131.2
(Pyr-CH), 128.2 (Tph-CH), 119.1 (Pyr-CH), 84.5(pin-C(CH3)4), 24.8 (pin-
C(CH3)4) ppm.3, 9 11B NMR (160 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 28.6 ppm. 19F NMR (470
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 73.0 ppm. M.p.: 121 °C. IR (ATR): ν = 2986(m), 1547 (w),
1531 (m), 1482 (w), 1421 (s), 1347 (s), 1321 (s), 1206 (s), 1135 (s),
1047 (m), 874 (m), 852 (m), 789 (m), 762 (m), 665 (m), 603 (s) cm-1. MS
(EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 516/514 (100)/(84) [M]+. MS (CI, isobutane): m/z
(%) = 516/514 (14)/(22) [M]+, 456/454 (100)/(98) [M - CF3O2S + H]+. HRMS
(ESI): m/z found 535.9608; calcd. for C16H16BBrF3NNaO5S2 535.9591.
