3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1-trityl-pyrazolo[3,4-b]pyridine
(3.71 g, 7.61 mmol), 2,6-dichloro-5-fluoronicotinonitrile (1.45 g, 7.61
mmol) and Na2CO3 (2.42 g, 22.84 mmol) were combined in toluene (46 mL),
water (12 mL), methanol (46 mL) and degassed by vacuum/nitrogen cycles (3
times). This mixture was then treated with Pd[P(Ph)3]4 (440 mg, 0.38
mmol) and then degassed again by vacuum/nitrogen cycles (2 times). The
reaction was heated at 120 °C for 6 h and allowed to cool to room
temperature. The reaction was diluted with DCM and the aqueous extracted
further with DCM. The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated to provide a solid that was slurried with
a 1:1 MeOH/DCM mixture and filtered to afford
2-chloro-5-fluoro-6-(1-trityl-1H-pyrazolo[3,4-b]pyridin-3-yl)nicotinonitrile.
3.2 g, 82 %. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 7.12 -7.41 (16H, m), 8.35 (1H, s), 8.69
-8.79 (2H, m). MS m/z: 516.1 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design and Optimization of Selective Protein Kinase C θ (PKCθ) Inhibitors
for the Treatment of Autoimmune Diseases
