$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Suzuki-Coupling Conditions. A solution
of dibromo compound 1a-d (1.00 eq) and
2-(5'-hexyl-2,2'-bithiophen-5-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
2 (3.00 eq) in a mixture of toluene/2 M aqueous Na2CO3 solution (4:1;
[dibromobenzotriazole] = 15 mM) and a few drops of Aliquat 336 was purged
with argon for about 1 h. Pd(PPh3)4 (~ 8 mol%) was added in one portion
and the mixture was refluxed until the starting material has been
consumed according to the TLC analysis. The reaction mixture was allowed
to cool to rt and diluted with MeOH to precipitate the desired product.
4,7-Bis(5'-hexyl-2,2'-bithiophen-5-yl)-2-(4-decyloxy-3,5-difluorophenyl)-2H-benzotriazole
(3c): Following the general Suzuki-coupling conditions starting from
4,7-dibromo-2-(4-decyloxy-3,5-difluorophenyl)-2H-benzotriazole (1c, 200
mg, 0.367 mmol) the reaction mixture was stirred 3 h at reflux
temperature. After precipitation with MeOH the solid residue was washed
with H2O, MeOH and acetone and then recrystallized from EtOAc to yield
the desired product as a red solid (262 mg, 81%).
4,7-Bis(5'-hexyl-2,2'-bithiophen-5-yl)-2-(4-decyloxy-3,5-difluorophenyl)-2H-benzotriazole
(3c), yield 262 mg, 81%. Mp = 145-147 °C. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm
8.09-7.80 (br, 4H), 7.43 (br, 2H), 7.12 (br, 2H), 7.06 (br, 2H), 6.71 (d,
J = 3.02 Hz, 2H), 4.22 (t, J = 6.50 Hz, 2H), 2.82 (t, J = 6.20 Hz, 4H),
1.82 (dq, J = 13.56, 6.63 Hz, 2H), 1.72 (dt, J = 15.30, 7.53 Hz, 4H),
1.54-1.47 (m, 2H), 1.46-1.23 (m, 24H), 0.93-0.88 (m, 9H). 13C NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm 156.09 (dd, J = 248.79, 6.83 Hz), 146.01, 142.81,
138.45, 137.58, 135.48 (dt, J = 222.79, 13.10 Hz), 134.86, 128.15,
125.04, 124.08, 123.81, 123.35, 123.25, 105.35-104.75 (m), 75.25 (t, J =
2.79 Hz) 32.08, 31.76, 31.74, 30.42, 30.19, 29.75, 29.52, 29.50, 28.99,
25.83, 22.86, 22.77, 14.29, 14.26. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm
-125.38 (s, 2F). MALDI HRMS m/z (M+) calcd for C50H59F2N3OS4+: 883.3504;
found 883.3511.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, quaternary ammonium compounds was used as catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
