$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
2-(5-halo-3-(6-methoxypyridin-3-yl)-2-methy1H-indo1-yl)acetate (I-14). To
a microwave vessel was added I-13 (1.3 mmol),
6-methoxypyridin-3-ylboronic acid (0.47 g, 3.1 mmol), PdCl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2
(49 mg, 0.07 mmol), and Cs2CO3 (2.0 g, 6.1 mmol) in DME (10.3 mL). The
contents were degassed with nitrogen and sealed. The reaction was heated
at 150 °C for 20 min in the microwave. The reaction was diluted with
EtOAc (250 mL) and washed with H2O (3 x 100 mL). The organic layer was
dried (MgSO4) and filtered. The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure, and the crude material was purified by silica gel column
chromatography. Methyl
2-(5-chloro-3-(6-methoxypyridin-3-yl)-2-methy1H-indo1-yl)-acetate
(I-14B). Intermediate I-14B was prepared according to the method
described for intermediate I-14A. 81% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
ppm 2.36 (s, 3 H), 3.72 (s, 3 H), 3.91 (s, 3 H), 5.21 (s, 2 H), 6.95 (d,
J=8.3 Hz, 1 H), 7.15 (dd, J=8.6, 2.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.41 (d, J=2.0 Hz, 1 H),
7.51 (d, J=8.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.80 (dd, J=8.6, 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.22 (d, J=2.5
Hz, 1 H)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, sealed vessel used, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Isoquinolinone Indole Acetic Acids as Antagonists of
Chemoattractant Receptor Homologous Molecule Expressed on Th2 Cells
(CRTH2) for the Treatment of Allergic Inflammatory Diseases
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kaila, Neelu; Follows, Bruce; Leung, Louis; Thomason, Jennifer; Huang,
Adrian; Moretto, Alessandro; Janz, Kristin; Lowe, Michael; Mansour, Tarek
S.; Hubeau, Cedric; Page, Karen; Morgan, Paul; Fish, Susan; Xu, Xin;
Williams, Cara; Saiah, Eddine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
