$DATUM Compound (2T-1): To a degassed solution of 5 (306.6 mg, 0.751 mmol), 3a
(336.4 mg, 0.894 mmol, 1.2 equiv) in distilled THF (60 mL) was added
Pd2dba3 (70.0 mg, 10 mol%), Cs2CO3 (500.3 mg, 1.536 mmol, 2.0 equiv) and
P(t-Bu)3 (0.30 mL, 40 mol%). The reaction medium was stirred at 35 °C for
18 h. The reaction was quenched with H2O, extracted with CH2Cl2, washed
with water, dried with brine and over Na2SO4. Purification on a silica
column chromatography using CH2Cl2/petroleum ether (30/70) as eluent
afforded the desired mono coupled product. Recrystallization from
CH2Cl2/EtOH afforded needles. Yield: 323.1 mg, 81%, red metallic needles.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 0.91 (t, 3H, 3J = 6.9 Hz), 1.31-1.42
(m, 6H), 1.68 (qt, 2H, 3J = 7.6 Hz), 2.48 (s, 3H), 2.80 (t, 2H, 3J = 7.6
Hz), 6.53 (dd, 1H, 3J = 4.3 Hz, 3J = 4.3 Hz), 6.72 (d, 1H, 3J = 3.6 Hz),
6.90 (s, 1H), 6.92-6.94 (m (d+dd), 2H), 7.07 (d, 1H 3J = 5.2 Hz), 7.23
(d, 1H, 3J = 5.2 Hz), 7.30 (dAB syst, 2H, 3J = 8.0 Hz), 7.45 (dAB syst,
2H 3J = 8.1 Hz), 7.90 (s, 1H), 7.95 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(ppm) = 14.2, 21.6, 22.7, 29.0, 30.4, 31.66, 31.73, 118.2, 124.5, 124.9,
127.7, 128.57, 128.62, 128.9, 129.3, 130.7, 130.8, 131.1, 132.0, 132.3,
135.0, 135.1, 141.5, 143.4, 143.9, 147.0, 147.9. 11B NMR (128.4 MHz,
CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 0.21 (t, JB-F = 28.8 Hz). EI-MS (m/z, relative
intensity): theoretical mass 530.18 (100); found 530.1 (100), 511.1 (15).
Anal. calcd for C30H29BF2N2S2 (Mr = 530.50): C, 67.97; H, 5.51; N, 5.28.
Anal. found: C, 67.72; H, 5.42; N, 5.09.
